{
  "iri": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_3720",
  "lang": "en",
  "description": [
    "The amide resulting from formal condensation of 4-amino-5-chloro-2-methoxybenzoic acid with <em>cis</em>-1-[3-(4-fluorophenoxy)propyl]-3-methoxypiperidin-4-amine. It has been used (as its monohydrate or as its tartrate) for the treatment of gastro-oesophageal reflux disease and for non-ulcer dyspepsia, but its propensity to cause cardiac arrhythmias resulted in its complete withdrawal from many countries, including the U.K., and restrictions on its use elsewhere."
  ],
